second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Where is the Red Brick School located?\", \"slot_hint\": \"place\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 116, \"text\": \"classes that were in Red Brick were relocated to parts of the previous middle school that had recently been vacated.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d00\", \"start\": 117, \"end\": 182, \"text\": \"The building slipped into a state of disrepair beginning in 1993.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d00\", \"start\": 183, \"end\": 278, \"text\": \"It was being used only for storage, and important problems, such as roof leaks, went unnoticed.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d00\", \"start\": 279, \"end\": 425, \"text\": \"Red Brick was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1998 by concerned residents who felt the building was in danger of destruction.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d00\", \"start\": 426, \"end\": 490, \"text\": \"In the 2000s, interest in redeveloping the building was sparked.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d00\", \"start\": 491, \"end\": 568, \"text\": \"Options varying from a community center, to senior apartments were discussed.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d00\", \"start\": 569, \"end\": 602, \"text\": \"In the end, the building was sold\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 116, \"text\": \"Classes that were in Red Brick were relocated to parts of the previous middle school that had recently been vacated.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d01\", \"start\": 117, \"end\": 182, \"text\": \"The building slipped into a state of disrepair beginning in 1993.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d01\", \"start\": 183, \"end\": 278, \"text\": \"It was being used only for storage, and important problems, such as roof leaks, went unnoticed.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d01\", \"start\": 279, \"end\": 452, \"text\": \"Red Brick, located in New York City, was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1998 by concerned residents who felt the building was in danger of destruction.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d01\", \"start\": 453, \"end\": 517, \"text\": \"In the 2000s, interest in redeveloping the building was sparked.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d01\", \"start\": 518, \"end\": 595, \"text\": \"Options varying from a community center, to senior apartments were discussed.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d01\", \"start\": 596, \"end\": 630, \"text\": \"In the end, the building was sold.\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 788, \"text\": \"﻿ Ontario Heritage Trust | Red Brick School , The Skip to content Menu Français Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn Search Sites Sites Conservation Property portfolio review Buildings Museums Easement properties Natural heritage Collections Archaeology Rentals x Programs Programs Provincial Plaque Program Doris McCarthy Artist-in-Residence Program Lieutenant Governor 's Ontario Heritage Awards Doors Open Ontario Heritage Week Premiers ' Gravesites Program Education and Outreach Intangible Cultural Heritage x Tools Tools Understanding adaptive reuse Collections database Plaque database Places of Worship Inventory Ontario Heritage Act Register Heritage Matters e-magazine Heritage Conservation Districts Conservation easements Local markers Tools for conservation Data inventories x\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 42, \"text\": \"located mostly within the Town of Oregon .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d03\", \"start\": 43, \"end\": 276, \"text\": \"Contents History Geography Demographics 2020 census 2010 census Education Notable people See also History South Main Street Historic District Oregon was settled in 1841 by Bartlet Runey , and the first house was constructed in 1843 .\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d03\", \"start\": 277, \"end\": 406, \"text\": \"Initially the settlement was known as `` Rome Corners , '' and there is a road south of the village which still bears that name .\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d03\", \"start\": 407, \"end\": 556, \"text\": \"When the Chicago and North Western Railroad came through the village in 1864 , their maps indicated a name of `` Oregon , '' and the name was adopted\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Red Brick School\", \"scope\": \"location\", \"claim\": \"The Red Brick School is located in New York City.\", \"answer\": \"New York City\", \"quote\": \"Red Brick, located in New York City, was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1998 by concerned residents who felt the building was in danger of destruction.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"Red Brick School\", \"scope\": \"location\", \"claim\": \"The Red Brick 